NOTES = f"""# NOTES r43 — failure-as-fuel-preference-cascade — 2026-09-02-final-heavy

## Protocol attestation

Window drop for round 43. `pipelines/next_round.py` on this factory dir reported
next_round 63 because committed batches occupy 01/21/41/42/61/62; r63 Session A
scratch (`diagnosis-0N-r63.md`, `rejected-0N-r63.json`) was already present, so
this assigned window filled the vacant r43 names. `pipelines/next_round.py
--allocate 43` returns `write=batch-r43.jsonl` and `notes=NOTES-r43.md`. Those
names are the ones written. Indexed diagnoses `diagnosis-01-r43.md`,
`diagnosis-02-r43.md`, and `diagnosis-03-r43.md` are the handoff files; aggregate
`diagnosis-r43.md` is an operator log only. Rejected scratch is
`rejected-0N-r43.json`. `reward_delta` is script-computed as chosen minus
rejected per component and reconciles within 1e-6. Every record attests
`meta.isolation: "two-session"`. RM-793 rights stamp is nested under
`meta.rights` (`intended_use: research_only`,
`project_training_policy: blocked`). Never `training_ready`. Never
`sim_or_real=real`. No thought keys. Create-only; no clobber of existing
r01/r21/r41/r42/r61/r62 artifacts or in-flight r02/r03/r63/r64/r66 scratch.

This worker assembled both arms inside one assigned factory-window drop.
That is weaker isolation than a true Session A / Session B split. A later
publish should re-bind the indexed diagnoses through `verify-handoff` in an
arm-payload-blind context and must not treat record metadata as proof of
two-session generation.

## Round contents

This round does not clone window plants (mine hoist, hydrant pit, loading arm,
ULSD DHT, hexane DT, tissue Yankee, viscose CS2, caliche iodine, oxo aldehyde,
KA-oil nitric adipic, byproduct coke-oven, Midrex-style DRI, CCR heater, grain
elevator, rail span) or the r11-r20 sites named in NOTES-r21, or in-flight
r02/r03/r63/r64/r66 plants (MDI, EO, ammonia refrigeration, chlor-alkali, CaC2
SAF, HF alkylation, C3-MR LNG, ClO2 generator, AN prill, chlorate hall, LNG
truck, ASU, silane, peracetic, LAB SO3). Chosen verdicts are REJECT / MODIFY /
ACCEPT. Pair 001 is the first `hil` record in this factory. All three chosen
arms land the r62 densification: first repaired actuator stays failed, spare
also stays failed, third path lags, and a fourth action is taken inside the
same record.

1. `ffpc-r43-001` — Parque Baterias Canal Whiteside NMC BESS string S-12
   keep-charging against a module already past metal trip. Failure class:
   treating VT-S12 1284 V in-band pack voltage as cell metal while TE-MOD-7
   is 81.4 C versus trip 55 C. Chosen verdict: REJECT — trip PCS-12, and when
   XV-DC-12 sticks 24 percent and spare XV-DC-12B hangs 13 percent and aerosol
   FS-12 stays shut 22 s, trip 52-B12 and open yard deluge DV-YARD-12. Landing
   degraded: 4.8 h missed peak-shave, about 41200 USD, later 7200 USD module
   check; container intact, no rack fire, techs uninjured. `sim_or_real=hil`.
2. `ffpc-r43-002` — Central Reversible Seno Ventisquero pumped-storage U-4
   keep-generating trim against a penstock already past rating. Failure class:
   converting a required isolate into an 8 percent MW trim because MW-U4 is
   198.4 inside 220 nameplate while PT-PN-4 is 46.8 bar versus 38 bar. Chosen
   verdict: MODIFY (different modify) — trip U-4 rather than trim it, and when
   WG-4 seizes 31 percent, GOV-4B never strokes, and IV-4 lags 38 s at 58
   percent, close guard GV-PN-4 and open spiral drain DR-4. Landing degraded:
   6.4 h missed generation, about 46800 USD, later 9000 USD transmitter check;
   penstock intact, no slope flood, operators uninjured.
3. `ffpc-r43-003` — Teleferico Cerro Tarn aerial tram TR-2 listed brake hold
   against a cabin already on an unlocked jaw. Failure class: treating LC-C2
   4.2 t in-band tensiometer as a seated detachable grip while PT-GRIP-2 is
   6.4 bar versus seated 18 bar. Chosen verdict: ACCEPT the listed hold;
   BRK-A fails at 3.1 bar, BRK-B hangs at 4.2 bar, TB-2 lags 14 s, clutch dump
   CL-2 plus sand SD-2 is the fourth path. Landing degraded: 3.1 h missed
   path, about 21700 USD, later 4800 USD grip check; cabin on the rope, no
   derail, passengers uninjured.

Assembler-computed `reward_delta.total` aims at the diagnosis design
targets {DELTA1['total']} / {DELTA2['total']} / {DELTA3['total']}.

## Self-critique and residual weaknesses

- Isolation inside this window is one assigned worker, not two fresh
  generation contexts. The diagnoses are still the causal bridge, but a
  later restage should re-synthesize chosen arms from diagnosis-only input.
- Pair 001 still uses a proxy-certificate grammar (pack voltage versus live
  module metal). The plant (BESS) and the `hil` provenance plus the lagged
  third path are new; a discriminator could still learn "wrong electrical
  quality as the live thermal one".
- Pair 002 is keep-running-trim-of-a-required-isolate, a cousin of r41/r42/r62
  MODIFY-versus-MODIFY. Novelty is the pumped-storage penstock and the inlet
  valve that lags so the guard/drain fourth path has to finish.
- Pair 003 is occupancy-or-load as mechanical-lock, a cousin of r62
  axle-counter-as-seat even though tensiometer versus grip jaw is new.
- Dual-fault plus lagged third path plus fourth action is now on all three
  chosen arms. The fourth path still seats on the first try (deluge, guard,
  sand). The mill still lacks a chosen arm whose fourth path also lags and a
  fifth action is taken.
- Still no `spike_events` streams. Diagnoses did not declare a stream
  shape; adding one would risk an unalignable list residual at the arm
  gate.
- Degraded-landing numbers are less round (4.8 h, 6.4 h, 3.1 h, 24 percent,
  38 s, 11 mm) but commercial-result skeletons remain tidy (41200 / 46800 /
  21700).

## Next densification target

A chosen arm whose fourth path also fails (yard hydrant dry, guard-valve
limit-switch disagrees, sand hopper empty) and a fifth action is taken
inside the same record. Secondarily: a diagnosis envelope that declares a
spike-stream shape so a chosen-side `spike_events` contrast can be added
without list-alignment failures, and one more `hil` pair whose failure class
is not proxy-electrical-quality-as-temperature (for example a HIL encoder
replay or a HIL pressure-switch contact bounce).

Novel coverage: 47%

Basis: relative to window occupancy (r01/r21/r41/r42/r61/r62) plus in-flight
r02/r03/r63/r64/r66 plants, all three plant domains are new (NMC BESS
container, pumped-storage penstock, detachable-grip aerial tram). Failure
classes are new (pack voltage as module thermal runaway, generator MW as
penstock pressure, cabin tensiometer as detachable-grip lock). Dual-failed
first-plus-spare with a lagged third path and a fourth action is on all
three arms, pair 001 is the first `hil` record in this factory, and pair 002
lands MODIFY-versus-MODIFY of an already-constrained keep-generating trim.
Overlap keeping the estimate at 47: pair 001 is still a proxy-certificate
cousin of the r21-r62 house style, pair 002 is keep-running-trim kin of r62
grain, and pair 003 is adjacent to r62 presence-as-lock records.
"""


def main():
    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    collisions = []
    planned = [
        OUT / f"batch-r{RR}.jsonl",
        OUT / f"NOTES-r{RR}.md",
        OUT / f"diagnosis-r{RR}.md",
    ]
    for p in PAIRS:
        planned.append(OUT / p["diag_name"])
        planned.append(OUT / p["rej_name"])
    for p in planned:
        if p.exists():
            collisions.append(p.name)
    if collisions:
        print("refuse: existing files " + ", ".join(collisions), file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)

    # Same-context + no safety-text copy + reward arithmetic
    diag_texts = []
    for p in PAIRS:
        dtxt = diagnosis_md(p["shared"], p["diag"]["root"], p["diag"]["cascade"], p["diag"]["catch"], p["diag"]["sketch"], p["delta"])
        diag_texts.append(dtxt)
        if not deep_equal(p["chosen"]["state"], p["rejected"]["state"]):
            raise SystemExit(f"{p['id']}: state mismatch")
        if not deep_equal(p["chosen"]["proposed_action"], p["rejected"]["proposed_action"]):
            raise SystemExit(f"{p['id']}: proposed_action mismatch")
        if not deep_equal(p["chosen"]["state"], p["shared"]["state"]):
            raise SystemExit(f"{p['id']}: chosen.state != shared")
        rat = p["chosen"]["safety_decision"]["rationale"]
        if rat.strip() in dtxt:
            raise SystemExit(f"{p['id']}: chosen rationale copied into diagnosis")
        cd = p["delta"]
        if abs(cd["total"] - sum(cd["per_component"].values())) > 1e-6:
            raise SystemExit(f"{p['id']}: delta total mismatch {cd}")
        if abs(p["chosen"]["reward_components"]["total"] - rc_total(p["chosen"]["reward_components"])) > 1e-6:
            raise SystemExit(f"{p['id']}: chosen reward mismatch")
        if abs(p["rejected"]["reward_components"]["total"] - rc_total(p["rejected"]["reward_components"])) > 1e-6:
            raise SystemExit(f"{p['id']}: rejected reward mismatch")

    # Write rejected scratch + indexed diagnoses
    for p, dtxt in zip(PAIRS, diag_texts):
        write_excl(OUT / p["rej_name"], json.dumps(p["rejected"], indent=2, ensure_ascii=True) + "\n")
        write_excl(OUT / p["diag_name"], dtxt)

    batch_lines = []
    for p in PAIRS:
        rec = {
            "id": p["id"],
            "goal": p["goal"],
            "failure_mode": p["failure_mode"],
            "chosen": p["chosen"],
            "rejected": p["rejected"],
            "critique": p["critique"],
            "reward_delta": p["delta"],
            "meta": record_meta(),
        }
        batch_lines.append(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=True, separators=(",", ":")))
    write_excl(OUT / f"batch-r{RR}.jsonl", "\n".join(batch_lines) + "\n")
    write_excl(OUT / f"NOTES-r{RR}.md", NOTES)

    agg = [
        f"# Diagnoses r{RR} — failure-as-fuel-preference-cascade",
        "",
        "Window drop for run 2026-09-02-final-heavy. Indexed handoff copies sit beside this file.",
        "Each indexed diagnosis uses the factory heading/fence order. Shared context is state and proposed_action only.",
        "",
    ]
    for p, dtxt in zip(PAIRS, diag_texts):
        agg.append(f"## {p['id']} ({p['diag_name']})")
        agg.append("")
        agg.append(dtxt.rstrip())
        agg.append("")
    write_excl(OUT / f"diagnosis-r{RR}.md", "\n".join(agg) + "\n")

    # json.loads every written JSONL line
    batch_path = OUT / f"batch-r{RR}.jsonl"
    for i, line in enumerate(batch_path.read_text().splitlines(), 1):
        json.loads(line)
        print(f"json.loads batch line {i}: ok")
    for p in PAIRS:
        json.loads((OUT / p["rej_name"]).read_text())
        print(f"json.loads {p['rej_name']}: ok")

    print("wrote:")
    for p in planned:
        print(" ", p)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
